\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Conductances do not choose the weights}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The energy of \ref{fdip-00EL} uses the conductances
#{\bigl(\frac{5}{3}\bigr)^n}. Those numbers do not appear in
#{\nu}. Any other positive triple summing to #{1} defines
another product on the same symbol space. Uniform counting
on the vertex set #{V_n} is a different assignment: it
charges vertices, whereas #{\nu} charges cylinders.}
